WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.596 --> 00:00:02.109
(orchestral music)

00:00:02.109 --> 00:00:04.444
- Very often people
think it's gonna be funny

00:00:04.444 --> 00:00:06.861
and then they realize it's not really.

00:00:06.861 --> 00:00:10.467
We really do music, it's not impossible

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:12.024
to make music with vegetables.

00:00:12.024 --> 00:00:15.774
(orchestral music continues)

00:00:17.389 --> 00:00:20.389
(audience applause)

00:00:22.573 --> 00:00:23.406
(pleasant music)

00:00:23.406 --> 00:00:25.437
My name is Susanna Gartmayer and I'm

00:00:25.437 --> 00:00:28.265
a member of the Vegetable Orchestra.

00:00:28.265 --> 00:00:32.035
The orchestra exists since 18 years now.

00:00:32.035 --> 00:00:34.494
The first instrument was the tomato

00:00:34.494 --> 00:00:37.827
because you can do sound with tomatoes

00:00:37.827 --> 00:00:40.242
but it will be messy, for sure.

00:00:40.242 --> 00:00:42.573
We go shopping on the market first.

00:00:42.573 --> 00:00:45.195
We choose all the vegetables there.

00:00:45.195 --> 00:00:47.816
We have three kinds of instruments.

00:00:47.816 --> 00:00:50.129
One is the ready-made, you can just

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:51.932
buy it at the market and play it.

00:00:51.932 --> 00:00:55.253
It's like the pepper, it's called, no?

00:00:55.253 --> 00:00:56.972
(squeaking of peppers)

00:00:56.972 --> 00:00:58.774
It's ready already.
(squeaking of peppers)

00:00:58.774 --> 00:01:01.472
And then there’re just
simple instruments like

00:01:01.472 --> 00:01:04.584
with one cut or some cuts.
(flapping of eggplants)

00:01:04.584 --> 00:01:07.577
We get it like that, then
with the more complex

00:01:07.577 --> 00:01:11.673
instruments we have some that
work like normal instruments.

00:01:11.673 --> 00:01:14.706
You know, the pumpkin is the bass drum

00:01:14.706 --> 00:01:18.267
and the sound of the
pumpkin is really important.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:19.619
- Good.

00:01:19.619 --> 00:01:22.160
- After shopping we go to the venue

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.743
and start to build instruments.

00:01:26.257 --> 00:01:27.965
(drills whirring)
All in all, it takes two

00:01:27.965 --> 00:01:31.938
to three hours to build all
the instruments for everybody.

00:01:31.938 --> 00:01:34.233
And then we start with the sound check.

00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:35.791
(whistle blowing)
And since we have new

00:01:35.791 --> 00:01:38.780
instruments each time, we have to have

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.263
a very long sound check.
(whistling of vegetables)

00:01:42.263 --> 00:01:45.263
(audience applause)

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.567
(tribal and orchestral-like music plays)

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.304
We have a lot of different

00:01:54.304 --> 00:01:56.679
musical influences in the orchestra.

00:01:56.679 --> 00:01:58.727
Since we're really many people,

00:01:58.727 --> 00:02:02.948
everybody's interested
in different things.

00:02:02.948 --> 00:02:05.244
We make a soup during the building process

00:02:05.244 --> 00:02:08.114
of the vegetable instruments with the

00:02:08.114 --> 00:02:10.121
remaining vegetables and we serve it

00:02:10.121 --> 00:02:12.537
to the audience after the concert.

00:02:12.537 --> 00:02:15.118
And it's also after hearing and seeing us

00:02:15.118 --> 00:02:17.015
and smelling the vegetables, which will be

00:02:17.015 --> 00:02:19.349
intense in there because
it's so small, this theater.

00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:21.766
And then you can also eat it.

00:02:22.668 --> 00:02:25.164
You never get it out of your head anymore

00:02:25.164 --> 00:02:29.464
if you're in the orchestra to
look vegetables in another way.

00:02:29.464 --> 00:02:32.464
(audience applause)

00:02:36.016 --> 00:02:39.683
(high pitched musical tone)

